# Quality

This is the authority for project-owned verification commands and the evidence expected from them. Reporivet does not wrap, execute, replace, or silently infer these commands as approved.

## Required checks and commands

{{QUALITY_EVIDENCE}}

Promote a Proposed command to Confirmed only after a project owner verifies its purpose, environment, side effects, and success criteria.

## Evidence contract

- Implementation agents report exact commands, outcomes, changed paths, discoveries, and residual risks.
- Verification agents use a fresh context, identify the integrated candidate, run applicable project-owned checks, and return criterion-level pass/fail evidence.
- Main judges sufficiency and updates the Plan; Main does not normally rerun detailed verification.
- Explanations and raw narration are not evidence. A passing command also does not prove criteria it did not exercise.

